 h_)/3 = (k+h_)/3.\n\n(3,4): neighbors (2,4)=h_, (4,4)=c, (3,3)=b, (3,5)=k. So j = (h_+c+b+k)/4.\n\n(3,5): neighbors (2,5)=i, (4,5)=l, (3,4)=j. So k = (i+l+j)/3.\n\n(4,5): neighbors (3,5)=k, (5,5)=0, (4,4)=c. So l = (k+0+c)/3 = (k+c)/3.\n\nThis is a 12-variable linear system. Let me solve it.\n\nEquations:\n(1) a = (d+g)/2\n(2) b = (g+j)/2\n(3) c = (j+l)/2\n(4) d = (1+a+e)/3\n(5) e = (d+g+f)/3\n(6) f = (e+h_)/3\n(7) g = (e+b+a+h_)/4\n(8) h_ = (f+j+g+i)/4\n(9) i = (k+h_)/3\n(10) j = (h_+c+b+k)/4\n(11) k = (i+l+j)/3\n(12) l = (k+c)/3\n\nThis is complex. Let me try to solve systematically. I'll use substitution.\n\nFrom (1): d = 2a - g.\nFrom (2): b = (g+j)/2.\nFrom (3): c = (j+l)/2.\n\nFrom (4): d = (1+a+e)/3 → 2a - g = (1+a+e)/3 → 6a - 3g = 1 + a + e → e = 5a - 3g - 1. ... (4')\n\nFrom (5): e = (d+g+f)/3 → 3e = d + g + f → f = 3e - d - g = 3(5a-3g-1) - (2a-g) - g = 15a - 9g - 3 - 2a + g - g = 13a - 9g - 3. ... (5')\n\nFrom (6): f = (e+h_)/3 → 3f = e + h_ → h_ = 3f - e = 3(13a-9g-3) - (5a-3g-1) = 39a - 27g - 9 - 5a + 3g + 1 = 34a - 24g - 8. ... (6')\n\nFrom (7): g = (e+b+a+h_)/4 → 4g = e + b + a + h_.\nb = (g+j)/2, so 4g = e + (g+j)/2 + a + h_ → 8g = 2e + g + j + 2a + 2h_ → 7g = 2e + j + 2a + 2h_.\nSubstitute e = 5a-3g-1, h_ = 34a-24g-8:\n7g = 2(5a-3g-1) + j + 2a + 2(34a-24g-8)\n7g = 10a - 6g - 2 + j + 2a + 68a - 48g - 16\n7g = 80a - 54g - 18 + j\n61g = 80a - 18 + j\nj = 61g - 80a + 18. ... (7')\n\nFrom (3): c = (j+l)/2 → l = 2c - j.\nFrom (12): l = (k+c)/3 → 3l = k + c → k = 3l - c = 3(2c-j) - c = 6c - 3j - c = 5c - 3j.\nc = (j+l)/2 = (j + 2c - j)/2 = c. OK consistent. So c = (j+l)/2 and l = 2c - j, k = 5c - 3j.\n\nFrom (2): b = (g+j)/2.\nFrom (10): j = (h_+c+b+k)/4 → 4j = h_ + c + b + k.\nSubstitute b = (g+j)/2, k = 5c - 3j:\n4j = h_ + c + (g+j)/2 + 5c - 3j\n4j = h_ + 6c + (g+j)/2 - 3j\n8j = 2h_ + 12c + g + j - 6j\n8j = 2h_ + 12c + g - 5j\n13j = 2h_ + 12c + g. ... (10')\n\nNow c = (j+l)/2 and l = 2c - j, k = 5c - 3j. We need another relation for c. From (3) c = (j+l)/2, and l from (12): l = (k+c)/3. And k = 5c - 3j. So l = (5c - 3j + c)/3 = (6c - 3j)/3 = 2c - j. Consistent, no new info.\n\nSo c is a free variable linked to j and l through (9), (11), (8).\n\nFrom (9): i = (k+h_)/3 = (5c - 3j + h_)/3.\nFrom (11): k = (i+l+j)/3 → 3k = i + l + j → i = 3k - l - j = 3(5c-3j) - (2c-j) - j = 15c - 9j - 2c + j - j = 13c - 9j. ... (11')\n\nSo from (9): i = (5c - 3j + h_)/3 = 13c - 9j → 5c - 3j + h_ = 39c - 27j → h_ = 34c - 24j. ... (9')\n\nFrom (8): h_ = (f+j+g+i)/4 → 4h_ = f + j + g + i.\nSubstitute f = 13a - 9g - 3, i = 13c - 9j:\n4h_ = 13a - 9g - 3 + j + g + 13c - 9j = 13a - 8g - 3 - 8j + 13c.\nh_ = (13a - 8g - 3 - 8j + 13c)/4. ... (8')\n\nNow I have expressions:\n- h_ = 34a - 24g - 8  (from 6')\n- h_ = 34c - 24j  (from 9')\n- j = 61g - 80a + 18  (from 7')\n- 13j = 2h_ + 12c + g  (from 10')\n- h_ = (13a - 8g - 3 - 8j + 13c)/4  (from 8')\n\nLet me use h_ = 34a - 24g - 8 and h_ = 34c - 24j:\n34a - 24g - 8 = 34c - 24j → 34a - 24g - 8 - 34c + 24j = 0. ... (A)\n\nFrom j = 61g - 80a + 18. ... (B)\n\nFrom 13j = 2h_ + 12c + g. Substitute h_ = 34c - 24j:\n13j = 2(34c - 24j) + 12c + g = 68c - 48j + 12c + g = 80c - 48j + g.\n61j = 80c + g. ... (C)\n\nFrom h_ = (13a - 8g - 3 - 8j + 13c)/4 and h_ = 34a - 24g - 8:\n34a - 24g - 8 = (13a - 8g - 3 - 8j + 13c)/4\n136a - 96g - 32 = 13a - 8g - 3 - 8j + 13c\n123a - 88g - 29 + 8j - 13c = 0. ... (D)\n\nNow I have 4 equations (A,B,C,D) in 4 unknowns (a, c, g, j).\n\n(A): 34a - 24g - 8 - 34c + 24j = 0 → 34a - 24g - 34c + 24j = 8.\n(B): j = 61g - 80a + 18.\n(C): 61j = 80c + g.\n(D): 123a - 88g - 29 + 8j - 13c = 0 → 123a - 88g + 8j - 13c = 29.\n\nSubstitute (B) into (A), (C), (D).\n\n(A): 34a - 24g - 34c + 24(61g - 80a + 18) = 8\n34a - 24g - 34c + 1464g - 1920a + 432 = 8\n-1886a + 1440g - 34c = -424\n1886a - 1440g + 34c = 424. ... (A')\n\n(C): 61(61g - 80a + 18) = 80c + g\n3721g - 4880a + 1098 = 80c + g\n3720g - 4880a + 1098 = 80c\nc = (3720g - 4880a + 1098)/80 = (1860g - 2440a + 549)/40. ... (C')\n\n(D): 123a